course: dictionary
lesson: 5598
title: One word, three meanings: lie
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word lie has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. «The lovely cart lies on its side» means the cart is resting flat, not that it is telling a story.
explain: Lie can mean to rest flat or to be in a place. «He lies awake feeling awful» means he is in bed, not sleeping. «The town lies by the sea» tells you where the town is.
explain: Lie can also mean to say something you know is not true, to trick someone. A lie is the thing that is said. Ask yourself: is this about a place or a position, or is someone trying to mislead? Then pick the meaning that fits the sentence.
fact: Lie can mean rest flat, be in a place, or say something false.
fact: «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side» means the cart rests flat on its side.
fact: A lie is a thing said that the speaker knows is false.
fact: A white lie is a small, kind lie, but telling lies still breaks trust.
fact: If you feel faint, lie down, which means rest flat.
exercise: «The town lies by the sea.» What does lies mean here? | Sleeps all day | Rests on a bed | *Is in a place | Tells a false story
exercise: «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» What does lies mean here? | Says something false | *Rests flat in bed, not sleeping | Is in a town by the sea | Is covered in sand
exercise: Ella says, «You told a lie.» What is a lie? | A kind word for a friend | *A thing said that the speaker knows is false | A flat bed for resting | A place where a town sits
test: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying, but it can hide things.» What does lying mean in this sentence? | *Saying something false to mislead | Resting flat on the ground | Being in a town by the sea | Sleeping late in the morning
test: What is a white lie? | A bed for the night | A big, angry shout | A lie told about snow | *A small, kind lie
exam: «Understanding the reason does not make the lie right.» Which meaning fits lie here? | Staying awake all night | Resting flat | *A false thing said to mislead | Being in a place
